  rt.1 8-10|table|Writes yesterday's events behind old baseball scores, correcting guesses if challenged
  rt.2 14-16|livingroom|Rests quietly while asking to make her own choices about help
  rt.3 20-22|radio|Asks permission to listen for usable news rather than having Kim summarize it
  bl.1 folded scorecard||A game attended with Ellen; a disputed error still has both their marks beside it.
  bl.2 scorecard pencil|Base.Pencil|Kept through leaving home; Connie treats it as hers even when everything else is borrowed.
  bl.3 baseball notebook|Base.Notebook|Old scores in front, outbreak days behind; she dislikes finding a guess recorded as certain.
  bl.4 useless room key|Base.KeyRing|Mavis changed the lock after eviction; Connie has not admitted the key no longer offers a home.
  bl.5 empty record sleeve||Protected Rex's sold record, now flattened inside the notebook as an explanation she avoids.
  bl.6 folded acceptance letter||An invented college place, no working instructions; Connie keeps it because destroying it feels like surrendering the real hope.
  rl.1 Kim Webb|mother|Found Connie after she left home; wants to help but frequently answers questions addressed to Connie.
  rl.2 Irene Hensley|grandmother|Called with two party-line rings and saved paper for Connie's scorekeeping.
  rl.3 Ellen Sykes|adult friend, nineteen|Shared ball games and challenged Connie's certainty about decisions off the field.
  rl.4 Mavis Trent|former landlady|Accused Connie falsely of theft but correctly discovered her invented college letter.
end

